# One build (WP3): the first-start battery question (apps/ipodui/
# battcell.h, screens/battq.c). Asked once, under the legal notice (the
# notice first); the wheel turns the drum, which stops at both ends;
# MENU, PLAY and the MENU hold do nothing; Select stores the answer
# (config.cfg "ipodui battery cell") and applies it: capacity, and the
# storage row scaled by the cell's sag, copied into the power thread's
# table (the "battery curve" line reads the table back). A reboot does
# not ask again and applies the stored answer at boot. Every other
# script runs pre-answered "3,000 mAh" (battcell.h), so their first
# frames never show it.
# The sim's own linear row (3,300 .. 4,300 mV, powermgmt-sim.c) is the
# base; 2,000 mAh = sag 10: 3300 3399 3795 4191 4290 (by hand:
# 3300 + (v - 3300) * 990 / 1000). This run is the 64 MB unit (the
# default; ipodui-battq-32.script is the 32 MB unit on the same binary).
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-battq.script
# env: IPODUI_SIM_BATTQ=clear
# env: IPODUI_SIM_NOTICE=clear
# golden: skip
# log: battq shown
# log: notice shown key=
# log: boot unit battery cell=unset mah=850 ram=64
# log: boot battery curve 3300 3400 3800 4200 4300 3200
# log: battq answered cell=2000
# log: battq unit battery cell=2000 mah=2000 ram=64
# log: battq battery curve 3300 3399 3795 4191 4290 3200
# log: boot unit battery cell=2000 mah=2000 ram=64
# log: boot battery curve 3300 3399 3795 4191 4290 3200
# nolog: hold MENU: to the main menu
# expect-file: /.rockbox/config.cfg ipodui battery cell: 2

# boot 1: nothing stored; the notice first, the question under it
wait 4500
shot notice
key SELECT           # the notice's Select (past its 3 s guard)
wait 1200
shot battq           # Stock in the box, 2,000 mAh peeking below
wheel +1
wait 600
shot battq-2000
wheel +1
wait 600
shot battq-3000      # the last value: nothing below
wheel +2             # stops at the end
wait 600
shot battq-end
key MENU             # nothing
wait 400
key PLAY             # nothing
wait 400
hold MENU 1200       # not "to the main menu" here
wait 600
shot battq-keys
wheel -1
wait 600
key SELECT           # answers 2,000 mAh
wait 1500
shot menu
reboot
# boot 2: answered; the Main Menu is the first frame
wait 4000
shot menu-next-boot
quit
